# remember — success
#
# REMEMBER exists only in the childhood-reminescence phase, so this test is the one that must NOT
# pass --skip-childhood: that flag skips the phase entirely and fills the starting kit as if it had
# run. Every other script in the suite passes it, which is why this verb had no test.
#
# The phase auto-succeeds by design — NarrativeController short-circuits it before the critic: no
# plausibility check, no noetic cost, dice at difficulty 0. So there is no `strategy` here and no
# meaningful failure case; `cli/remember/` has one script, deliberately.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue

# The phase opens on its own — no travel, no location. Wait for the mode rather than for idleness.
wait mode ChildhoodReminescence 60
advance 12 180
regions

# A memory fragment is the observable, and REMEMBER is the only verb the phase offers.
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
regions

click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

# What makes this a remember test rather than an any-verb test.
expect-verb remember
quit
